From b8fa036e3a64ffee2c52a52aa18fab31c7ae7ec3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sathishkumar Muruganandam <murugana@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Jun 2026 16:42:18 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] wifi: ath12k: clean up failed MLO STA vdev start

During MLO STA authentication, mac80211 sets vif->valid_links before the
STA vdev is successfully started. If firmware rejects WMI_VDEV_START,
ath12k leaves the created link vdev around because chanctx unassign only
removes link interfaces when vif->valid_links is zero.

This leaves stale created-but-not-started vdevs after failed auth
attempts, causing retries to allocate new vdev IDs and repeatedly fail
vdev start.

Clean up STA link vdevs that were created but never started, even when
vif->valid_links is still set.

Signed-off-by: Sathishkumar Muruganandam <murugana@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c | 19 ++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
index b804d0342ff2..79ffae20b6ff 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -19280,14 +19280,19 @@ ath12k_mac_unassign_vif_chanctx_handle(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 		ar->state_11d = ATH12K_11D_PREPARING;
 	}
 
-	/* In legacy station association with the AP,
-	 * arvif is created during channel context assignment.
-	 * However, since mac80211 is unaware of this link,
-	 * it is not deleted automatically. To prevent stale arvif
-	 * entries in ahvif, this link must be explicitly removed
-	 * during channel context unassignment.
+	/* In legacy station association with the AP, arvif is created during
+	 * channel context assignment. However, since mac80211 is unaware of this
+	 * link, it is not deleted automatically. To prevent stale arvif entries
+	 * in ahvif, this link must be explicitly removed during channel context
+	 * unassignment.
+	 *
+	 * For MLO station association failures, mac80211 may still have
+	 * vif->valid_links set when the link vdev was created but never started.
+	 * Remove it here as well, otherwise failed auth retries leak stale vdevs.
 	 */
-	if (!vif->valid_links) {
+	if (!vif->valid_links ||
+	    (ahvif->vdev_type == WMI_VDEV_TYPE_STA &&
+	     arvif->is_created && !arvif->is_started)) {
 		ath12k_mac_remove_link_interface(hw, arvif);
 		ath12k_mac_unassign_link_vif(arvif);
 	}
